cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Author names, ORCID iDs and the journal reference are withheld while the
  accompanying manuscript is under anonymized peer review, and will be added on
  acceptance. Until then, please cite this software by its title and repository
  address.
title: "CT-FFR Research Inference Application"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-08
authors:
  - name: "The authors of the accompanying CT-FFR prediction study"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ruihaomei/ctffr-app"
abstract: >-
  Local-first web, command-line and Python application for inference from a
  locked gradient boosting model that estimates CT-derived fractional flow
  reserve from routine coronary CT angiography measurements. For academic
  research use only; not a medical device and not for clinical decision-making.
keywords:
  - coronary computed tomography angiography
  - fractional flow reserve
  - machine learning
  - reproducible research
